WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.545
The revolt of 1857 was crushed.

2
00:00:03.912 --> 00:00:05.652
Yet it ended the East India

3
00:00:05.652 --> 00:00:06.618
Company's rule.

4
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.097
On 10 May 1857, sepoys at

5
00:00:10.097 --> 00:00:11.612
Meerut rose,

6
00:00:11.932 --> 00:00:13.108
and marched to Delhi.

7
00:00:13.443 --> 00:00:15.331
Rebels proclaimed Bahadur

8
00:00:15.331 --> 00:00:17.370
Shah Zafar, the last Mughal

9
00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:18.956
ruler, their emperor.

10
00:00:19.301 --> 00:00:21.181
The trigger: new cartridges,

11
00:00:21.181 --> 00:00:22.994
reportedly greased with cow

12
00:00:22.994 --> 00:00:23.800
and pig fat.

13
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.112
Behind it: annexations, and

14
00:00:26.112 --> 00:00:27.328
long grievances.

15
00:00:27.765 --> 00:00:28.593
Why did it fail?

16
00:00:29.041 --> 00:00:30.603
It stayed mostly in the north

17
00:00:30.603 --> 00:00:31.196
and centre,

18
00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:33.407
with no single plan or leader,

19
00:00:33.717 --> 00:00:35.430
and many rulers sided with

20
00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:37.340
a better-armed British force.

21
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:40.113
In 1858, an Act of Parliament

22
00:00:40.113 --> 00:00:42.482
moved power from the Company

23
00:00:42.482 --> 00:00:43.582
to the Crown.

24
00:00:43.928 --> 00:00:45.234
A lost revolt.

25
00:00:45.618 --> 00:00:46.848
A changed Raj.

26
00:00:47.653 --> 00:00:48.360
Your turn.

27
00:00:48.869 --> 00:00:51.251
What did the Government of

28
00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:52.991
India Act, 1858 do?
